<title>ITALY: Olivetti opens 3.5 pct down in Milan.</title>
<headline>Olivetti opens 3.5 pct down in Milan.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Crisis-hit information technology group Olivetti opened 3.58 percent down on the Milan stock market at a new record low of 498 lire per share.</p>
<p>The loss-making company was struck by a fresh negative development late on Monday when Italian bourse watchdog Consob said it had asked Olivetti to supply answers on Tuesday to 16 points it wants clarified regarding the group's financial performance.</p>
<p>Consob has already asked for clarification of the state of Olivetti's finances.</p>
